### Expense Tracker API — sample requests
### Base URL
@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health check
GET {{base}}/health

### Create an expense
POST {{base}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Coffee", "amount": 4.5, "category": "food" }

### Create another expense
POST {{base}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Monitor", "amount": 100, "category": "office" }

### List all expenses
GET {{base}}/expenses

### Filter by category
GET {{base}}/expenses?category=food

### Filter by max amount
### BUG-001: before the fix, string/number coercion makes this return wrong results.
GET {{base}}/expenses?maxAmount=9

### Get expense by id (replace the id)
GET {{base}}/expenses/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### Get a non-existent expense
### BUG-002: before the fix, this returns 200 + empty body instead of 404.
GET {{base}}/expenses/does-not-exist

### Summary (total + per-category)
GET {{base}}/summary

### Filter endpoint
### SEC-001: before the fix, `expr` is passed to eval() — code injection / RCE.
### Benign example:
GET {{base}}/expenses/filter?expr=e.amount > 10
### Malicious example (DO NOT run against a real process — demonstrates the vuln):
# GET {{base}}/expenses/filter?expr=process.exit(1)
